{"id": "EUVD-2026-97002", "enisaUuid": "e466cb45-5f79-3775-965f-01bc50a02b86", "description": "phpMyFAQ through 4.1.10 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the MCP server faq_search tool that allows MCP clients to read restricted FAQs because Search::searchDatabase() never applies user or group permission checks. Attackers connected to the phpmyfaq:mcp:server can issue search queries to retrieve the full question and answer text of active FAQs restricted to specific users or groups.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:26:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:39:25", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/phpmyfaq-mcp-search-visibility", "https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/blob/4.1.10/phpmyfaq/src/phpMyFAQ/Search.php#L137-L194", "https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/blob/4.1.10/phpmyfaq/src/phpMyFAQ/Service/McpServer/FaqSearchToolExecutor.php#L56-L102", "https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-through-4.1.10-missing-authorization-via-mcp-server-faq-search-tool"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108851", "GHSA-52xr-g583-rx96"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "444d3233-2ee7-3a64-828c-885caf76b277", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.1.0 \u22644.1.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "490724a5-8aee-35b7-a96d-d0f58e2d862a", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}